From 2530ce628a840a8678ff9ffa5d2f5229e91d640a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:34:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/43] hid: take mouse buttons from all reports of the
 collection

Some mice send buttons and wheel in one HID report and the X/Y axes in
another. The CHERRY DW 9100 Slim (USB 046a:c114) uses report ID 1 for
buttons, wheel and pan, and report ID 2 for 12 bit X and Y. The mouse
protocol handler only looked for buttons in the report that holds X
and Y, so the pointer moved but clicks and the wheel were never seen.

Add MouseReportDecoder. It finds buttons, wheel and pan in all input
reports of the mouse collection and keeps the button state and the
click count across reports. HIDParser::SetReport now hands the data to
the report that arrived first and only then notifies the others.
The new source is added to the Jamfiles of usb_hid, i2c_hid,
bluetooth_hid and hyperv_hid, which all build the mouse handler.

Mice that send everything in one report behave as before.

Signed-off-by: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: claude-sonnet-5-5
(cherry picked from commit 59f97cd02e65cc3553065eb5a3e1a903d33a6557)
